# Input for the hash-pinned requirements.txt: every THIRD-PARTY dependency of the packages under
# packages/ and admin/ (the redblue-* ones are installed from this repository, editable, never from
# PyPI), the development tools of `make dev`, and the build backend the packages declare.
#
# Regenerate requirements.txt after changing this file or any package's dependencies:
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --python-version 3.11 --only-binary :all: \
#     --generate-hashes --no-header -o requirements.txt
#
# --universal: one file for every Python RedBlue supports (3.11+) and every platform, with markers.
# --only-binary: wheels only; a dependency published only as source cannot be locked here.
# tests/test_requirements.py fails when a package depends on something not listed here.

